## Key Learning

CPU and Memory Hot Plug behave differently on Linux systems. While Ubuntu typically recognizes newly added memory immediately, additional virtual 
CPUs may remain **offline** even after a successful hypervisor upgrade. Administrators should verify CPU status using the Linux CPU hotplug 
interface and manually enable offline processors when necessary. This approach allows production systems to benefit from online CPU expansion 
without requiring a reboot.


